# The serving configuration, in one file, because it is the thing that has to be reproducible.
#
# Everything here is a decision with a measurement behind it in notes/SPEED-LEDGER.md; the ones
# that are not obvious:
#
#   LEN_FIXED=0    with LEN_LATCH=1: the drafter policy. Deciding the block width once a REQUEST
#   LEN_LATCH=1    rather than once a block. Per-block routing lost to a fixed sixteen in three
#                  consecutive phases, and the phase-9 control says why: switching arms costs
#                  acceptance whether or not the switch was a good idea (00:50). Four wide blocks,
#                  up to four narrow probes, one decision, then no more switching.
#   MAX_LEN        the KV buffer is allocated for all of it at load. Measured 2026-09-18 (P0,
#                  tools/mem_audit.py): 64 KiB a token of engine KV + 20 KiB a token for each of
#                  the two drafter arms = 106.5 KiB a token, 27.9 GB of KV at 256k, and 53.45 GB
#                  for the whole served stack in a fresh process. The "~0.5 MB a token" this file
#                  carried until that measurement was wrong by eight.
#   CACHE_GB       the state cache's budget, after the KV has been paid for.
#   FUSE_PROJ=0    the fused projection groups are lossless and worth ~1 % (phase 9, 00:58). They
#                  are OFF in the release candidate because the candidate is a stability release;
#                  set to 1 to measure them.
HOME_DIR=${HOME}
REPO=${HOME}/qwen38-spark-engine
PY=${HOME}/recipes/ling3-flash-dgx-spark/.venv/bin/python
PYTHONPATH=${HOME}/pylibs

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8000
SERVED_MODEL=qwen38-spark-engine

NV=${HOME}/nvfp4/mlp-clip.safetensors,${HOME}/nvfp4/gdn-clip.safetensors,${HOME}/nvfp4/attn-clip.safetensors
HEAD=${HOME}/nvfp4/head-fp8.safetensors
CKPT8=${REPO}/train/ft-b8-v2
CKPT16=${REPO}/train/ft-b16
CORPUS=${REPO}/corpus

MAX_LEN=262144
DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=16384
# Anti-repetition (ENG-17). All empty/absent = the server defaults, which are the identities:
# penalties off, no pattern stop, byte-identical output. Per-request body params
# (`repetition_penalty`, `presence_penalty`, `frequency_penalty`) override the server defaults --
# Open WebUI model rows that already send `presence_penalty` are honoured the moment the engine
# restarts, so check the roster's values before flipping anything here.
#REP_PENALTY=1.05
#PRESENCE_PENALTY=1.0
#FREQUENCY_PENALTY=0.0
# 64:4:16, not 64:1:8: the 1-token/8-repeat floor cut a legitimate generated code file
# mid-line on 2026-09-18 (a formatting cycle, not a loop). Loops that matter are
# handled by no_repeat + the think-stall signal + the budget; the guard is the last
# resort and must be conservative.
PATTERN_STOP=64:4:16
REASONING_FORMAT=tags
REASONING_EFFORT=medium
LEN_FIXED=0
LEN_LATCH=1
BUDGET=16
CACHE_GB=24
REQUEST_TIMEOUT=900
MAX_QUEUE=8
QUEUE_TIMEOUT=120
FUSE_PROJ=0

# Set explicitly so the serving configuration is readable in one place even where it agrees with
# the code default. Both were tried, and the row turned out not to be able to resolve either of
# them -- two runs of the same engine differ by 10 % on the mean (phase 9, 02:52). They are at the
# values the release candidate was soaked on, and they go to the `speed` branch to be measured
# against several rows each.
QWEN38_DF2_TREE_MODE=paths
QWEN38_TREE_ALIAS_STATE=0

# PHASE 10, 2026-09-18. Release the arm that loses the latch: no tap, no sync, and nothing of it in
# the state snapshot. Lossless (tools/verify_spec.py --drop-idle reports `identical` on every
# workload), and on the paired five-workload bench it is ahead of the router on 15 of 15
# comparisons -- five workloads times three repeats -- for a median of +3.2 % and a mean of +4.0 %,
# with accepted-per-block equal or better everywhere. The saving is largest exactly where the
# engine is fastest, because what stops is a `sync` over the ACCEPTED rows: +1.5 % on prose at 2.7
# accepted a block, +7.1 % on edit at 12.6.
DROP_IDLE=1
